---
title: Installation
description: Add Formsnap and its peer dependencies, then satisfy the version ranges Superforms and zod impose.
---

<script>
	import { Callout } from "$lib/markdown";
</script>

Formsnap is a component library, not a form runtime. You install it alongside Superforms, which owns loading, validation and submission, and a schema library for the validator adapter.

## Install

```bash
pnpm add @emmorts/formsnap sveltekit-superforms zod
```

```bash
npm install @emmorts/formsnap sveltekit-superforms zod
```

```bash
yarn add @emmorts/formsnap sveltekit-superforms zod
```

```bash
bun add @emmorts/formsnap sveltekit-superforms zod
```

## Requirements

| Dependency             | Supported range                                     |
| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `svelte`               | `^5.30.2`                                           |
| `sveltekit-superforms` | `^2.19.0` or `^3.0.0` — `./remote` does not need it |
| `@sveltejs/kit`        | `^3.0.1` — the `./remote` entry point only          |
| schema library         | any Superforms adapter; these docs use zod          |

Superforms 3 additionally requires Svelte `^5.56.4`; the Svelte 5.30.2 minimum applies to Formsnap with Superforms 2.

`@sveltejs/kit` and `sveltekit-superforms` are both optional peers. The root entry point still needs Superforms, exactly as before; the `@emmorts/formsnap/remote` entry point presents a native Kit remote form and needs Kit with `experimental.remoteFunctions` enabled, and nothing Superforms-shaped. See [Remote forms](/docs/recipes/remote-forms) before installing for that entry, because the version that carries it is not published yet.

<Callout type="warning">

Under `sveltekit-superforms` 2.31 and later, the zod adapter is typed against the zod v3 API exposed at `zod/v3`. Import your schema from `zod/v3`, and keep exactly one zod version in your dependency tree — pnpm can install a second copy for Superforms' own dependencies. Check with `pnpm why zod`.

</Callout>

## Import

Components and hooks come from the package root:

```ts title="src/routes/settings/settings-form.svelte"
import { Control, Description, Field, FieldErrors, Fieldset, Label, Legend, ElementField } from "@emmorts/formsnap";
import { useFormControl, useFormField } from "@emmorts/formsnap";
```

A native SvelteKit remote form comes from its own entry point, which needs no Superforms:

```ts title="src/routes/orders/order-form.svelte"
import { Label, RemoteControl, RemoteField, RemoteFieldset } from "@emmorts/formsnap/remote";
```

